  "text": "I'm so sorry to hear that you're feeling angry and sad. It's completely normal to feel that way when we feel like our parents are trying to control us.\n\nWhen I was in a similar situation, I remember feeling really frustrated and angry too. But what helped me was talking to my mom about how I felt. I told her that I understood she was coming from a place of love and concern, but that I also needed some space to make my own choices.\n\nIt wasn't easy, and we didn't always see eye to eye. But over time, we started to have more open and honest conversations about what was bothering me. I learned that it was okay to disagree with her, and that she was willing to listen to me and try to understand my perspective.\n\nIt might not be the same for you, and that's okay. But I want you to know that you're not alone in feeling this way. It's okay to feel angry and sad, and it's okay to express those feelings to your mom.\n\nIf you feel comfortable, can you tell me more about what's been going on with your mom and the friends you want to have? Sometimes talking about it can help clarify things and give us a sense of what we need to do next.\n\nAlso, I want to remind you that you do have the freedom to choose your friends. Your mom might not agree with your choices, but ultimately, it's up to you to decide who you want to surround yourself with.\n\nYou are loved, you are valued, and you are worthy of having friends who make you happy.",
